{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>These are the words</b> alludes to 3 times: they were said at Sinai, repeated in the Tent of Meeting, and triplicated in the plains of Moab. And for each and every commandment, 16 covenants were cut at Sinai, 16 in the Tent of Meeting, and 16 in the plains of Moab — totalling 48. Corresponding to these, the Torah warns 48 times about idolatry, and warns 48 times in the Torah about the convert who comes to cleave to the Torah — for 48 covenants were cut upon it." "<b>בראשית ואלה ויקרא וידבר אלה</b> — ס\"ת in gematria יראת, this is \"the fear of YHWH is the beginning of wisdom,\" and in gematria תורה. ר\"ת of the five books: ב' ו' ו' ו' א' in gematria אהיה. And the final letters of the five books: מ' מ' י' ו' ל' in gematria הוא אלהינו, and this is \"and the last things — I am He.\"" "<b>מול</b> — 2 times; and the other: \"מול את בני\" etc. Five things are said of a reed: one may not circumcise with it, and one may not cut flesh with it, and one may not slaughter with it, as stated in tractate Chullin. And this is what the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Joshua: \"Make yourself flint swords\" and do not circumcise with the reed that grows at the end of a marsh — and this is מול סוף. \"מול את בני ישראל.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The five initials (בווא) correspond to the first letters of בראשית, ואלה (Exodus), ויקרא (Leviticus), וידבר (Numbers), אלה (Deuteronomy); the five final letters (ממיל) correspond to the last letters of each book's final word.", 2 "The second occurrence of מול referenced is Joshua 5:2; the phrase מול סוף is read as a notarikon hint connecting to the reed (קנה) at the end (סוף) of a marsh (אגם)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:08:32.574768498Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}